939:
(a) The producer of a film production shall make application for a permit for the film production on a form prescribed by the city.
(b) An application for a film production permit shall be filed at least seven days prior to the date the film production is scheduled to begin in a residential area and 48 hours in advance of film production for all other locations; provided, however, no application shall be accepted earlier than one year prior to the date film production is scheduled to begin.
(c) The director may waive the deadline for filing an application if there is sufficient time to process the application and for the department to prepare for the requested filming activity. The director will also determine any additional fees incurred due to any costs associated with expedited processing of the permit application.
(d) All producers of a film production shall be properly identified on the application; provided, however, a film production permit shall be issued only to an individual person. Therefore, if a group, organization, association, or other entity is producing the film production, a designated agent of the producer shall be named for purposes of the permit, and this individual shall be solely and fully responsible for compliance with all provisions, including all financial requirements of this article and other applicable laws and ordinances.
(e) Each city department and/or agency whose services would be impacted by the film production shall review the application and recommend in writing any conditions or restrictions deemed necessary. The city or any of its departments may require any other information deemed reasonably necessary to determine that the permit meets the requirements of this article. All special conditions or restrictions recommended by any of the city departments, city manager, or their designees, shall become a condition of the permit.
(f) The application for a film production permit shall include the following information:
(1) Project title;
(2) Type of production;
(3) Event details and description;
(4) Name, address, e-mail address, and telephone number of the producer and the sponsoring entity or person in addition to the person named in subsection (d) of this section;
(5) Dates, locations, and hours of filming;
(6) Business license;
(7) Payment of all fees;
(8) Detailed description of each element of filming including but not limited to the elements listed in section 15-563 (b) regardless of whether the film location is on public or private property;
(9) All applicable insurance information and certificates;
(10) Overall site plan of the filming location. Plan must be drawn to scale and must include:
a. All property boundaries and setbacks for proposed location of the film production;
b. All existing buildings, structures, parking, and curb cuts permanently located on site; and
c. Any proposed temporary structures including buildings, structures, and parking;
(11) Projected attendance during film production;
(12) Plans for parking, restroom facilities, and sanitation concerns;
(13) First aid/medical support plan;
(14) Plan for crowd and traffic control;
(15) Plan for clean-up and close out of all locations used for filming;
(16) List of all vehicles used as part of or incidental to filming and all dates and times of use;
(17) Total number of personnel involved in filming including but not limited to crew, case, models and extras;
(18) Staging area plan;
(19) Proposed street/parking plan;
(20) Proposed street/parking lot closure plan;
(21) Proposed traffic plan (if necessary);
(22) Proposed equipment and sound amplification plan;
(23) Producer shall provide proof that all affected residents/businesses both on and adjacent to a proposed street closure are to be notified seven days prior to the proposed filming as required in the application form provided by the department. The department shall provide the list of affected residents/businesses to the producer. The event producer shall provide residents/businesses a copy of the proposed street closure map. Additionally, notification signs may be required at the producer's expense in the neighborhood during the street closure for traffic routing purposes.
(Ord. No. 2018-10-06, 10-23-2018)

